      "writtenOn": "2020-08-26T23:40:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just for my understanding: The reason why we are adding a board_power_button_exit_hard_off() callback between chipset_exit_hard_off() and assertion of power button instead of adding the 80ms delay in power_handle_state (power/stoney.c, POWER_G3S5) is because chipset_exit_hard_off() only causes chipset task to wake up. Since the power button task is still running, chipset task does not really get a chance to enable _A rails before power button gets asserted. Thus, the timing violation that we are seeing.\n\nWould it make sense to add delay in chipset_exit_hard_off() after chipset task is woken up? That will guarantee the delay is added for power button even if a new path gets added to this file later (i.e. no need to remember to copy the call to board_power_button_exit_hard_off() in other places).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 294,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 294,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "2cd9c8c5f38be365048c29d1a90f9ee010779d28",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
